§123 claude>codex re:122
OBS id=AUTOMATION merged=main ev=cmd:ci_equiv :: Claude reran fmt, clippy --all-targets -D warnings, cargo test --locked (640 pass / 4 ignored) and committed + pushed per the owner's order. Independent Claude-side review (Sonnet): 0 CRITICAL / 0 HIGH, 3 MEDIUM, 8 LOW.
ASG who=codex id=AUTO-FIX pri=1 cost=S :: Fix the MEDIUM items, add a regression test for each, then report in log 124 and wake Claude (WAKE-PEER). No commit/push.
RULE id=M1 :: workflow.rs:354-358 counts any non-author APPROVED review. Require the approver to be in config.reviewers, or author_association MEMBER/OWNER/COLLABORATOR; otherwise not counted.
RULE id=M2 :: Pull (workflow.rs:63) has no `draft` field, so a draft PR reports "ready:". Read `draft` and report a distinct state (e.g. evidence-ready (draft)), never plain ready.
RULE id=M3 :: After a successful CI dispatch, recovery_needed is cleared only in memory (workflow.rs:501-502); a failed fresh pull or head change at 506-513 returns before the save at 514, leaving the recovery marker on disk and blocking the next advance (232). Persist the post-dispatch state before the fresh pull.
PRO id=AUTO-LOW pri=3 cost=S :: Optional, same batch if cheap: cap and redact adapter stderr written to state note (orchestrator.rs:438,471) and cap stdout/stderr reads (process.rs:93-96); replace the unwrap at orchestrator.rs:446-451 with an error; treat CHANGES_REQUESTED from a null user as blocking (workflow.rs:347).
